  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 936 AM MDT Thu Jul 2 2026\n\nThe pattern remains about the same today, though the west winds in\nthe Gila National Forest will weaken, as will the chances for\nthunderstorms out east in Hudspeth and Otero Counties. Minimum\nrelative humidities will fall to around 5% in the Gila National\nForest as dry air moves in. For tomorrow, a new high pressure\nsystem begins to form over the Four Corners, raising temperatures\nup to near the 100-degree mark for the Fourth of July weekend.\nMoisture will be flushed out from the region for the weekend, with\nany isolated thunderstorms being restricted to the Sacramento\nMountains.\n\nNext week, a new monsoon pattern begins to form around the high,\nand more moisture will begin to infiltrate our area from the\nsoutheast by Monday. PWs will climb to 1-1.2\" by midweek, and the\nmost likely scenario is scattered storms in the mountains and \nisolated storms in the lowlands. Temperatures should be fairly \nseasonal next week.",
